        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Set of vestments consisting of a chasuble, stole, burse and chalice veil, all of embroidered velvet, designed by Augustus Welby Northmore Pugin, England, ca. 1850."@en , "Set of vestments consisting of a chasuble, stole, burse and chalice veil. They are all of red velvet, lined with red silk and embroidered with applied cloth of gold, velvet, silk and gold thread, purl, bullion and cord with floss and twisted silks. They are partially padded, with additional glass beads and seed pearl decoration."@en ;
